<%#
  Session 16 — human escalation surfaced as a state of the estimate.

  The decision is NOT made here. The AI service's deterministic output guardrail
  already decided, and this partial routes on it. Re-deriving the verdict in the
  platform would give two answers to one question, and the one written in the
  audit log would be the other one.

  Rendered only when the subject carries a number the guardrail doubts. An
  abstention is not a review case: the system declining to answer is the system
  working, and sending every abstention to a person trains reviewers to
  rubber-stamp the whole queue.

  The local is ``subject:`` and not ``estimate:`` because more than one thing can
  be flagged: the RAG estimate, the wizard's derived hours, a graph run. All three
  answer ``needs_review?`` and ``review_reasons``; naming the local after just one
  of them would be a lie about the type.

  ``respond_to?`` is deliberate belt-and-braces: a run persisted before Session 16
  must render without the banner, not raise.
%>
<% if subject.respond_to?(:needs_review?) && subject.needs_review? %>
  <div class="mb-5 rounded-md border border-amber-400/40 bg-amber-400/10 p-4"
       role="status" aria-live="polite">
    <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <svg class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-amber-300 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24"
           stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
              d="M12 9v4m0 4h.01M10.29 3.86 1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z" />
      </svg>
      <div class="flex-1">
        <p class="text-sm font-bold tracking-tight text-amber-200">
          Esta estimación necesita revisión humana
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-white/60">
          El servicio IA la ha entregado igualmente — no se descarta trabajo ya pagado —
          pero sus comprobaciones deterministas no la avalan.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1.5">
          <% subject.review_reasons.each do |reason| %>
            <li class="flex gap-2 text-xs text-white/80">
              <span class="text-amber-300/70" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <span><%= reason %></span>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
